ii. 	To elaborate on what I touched on earlier, there have been many examples of this 
exact question of a definition for a myth being asked, though without an easy answer. 
For other people’s definitions of myths, I mainly searched Discord in RMH’s server, 
where I found countless people asking, likely joking, without a response. Most of these 
also took place years ago, and not too many people ask the question. Some receive the 
answer that a myth is like a Roblox creepypasta, or that it is just someone mysterious, or 
that you are a myth if you say you are. To me, these feel too flimsy and ill-defined. One 
resorted to MEE6, an AI, which answered with a simple definition: a myth is a mystery 
that pervades the thoughts of many, whether character or game, just something 
mysterious. I think shifting the concept away from anything tangible is also flimsy, and it 
also adds in ARGs and legends with myths, which I believe to be too different from what 
is considered a myth. These theories are from more recent years, around 2023, though 
when I look further back, the more fractured and less clear answers become.  Tons of 
messages asking what a myth is are ignored, but to think from an observer’s perspective, 
they could assume it was someone trolling or begging for attention, or maybe the concept 
of a myth didn’t need much thought back then; a myth simply being a place with secrets or 
lore worked. I’ve looked through RMH for all cases of a definition of a myth, and it’s surprisingly 
small. Every definition here serves the purpose to convey what a myth feels like, but I don’t 
think they can strictly define a myth; there are myths that do not fit these definitions, 
and so are not considered true myths. My definition aims to reduce this exclusion to 
something felt by a lot of the community; that characters on Roblox are not inherently 
myths. What is most solid ends up leaning toward simplicity, one conversation in the 
middle of 2023, which was then used to define a myth in the myth community wiki at 
some point. It defines a myth as one or more people representing a story or idea with 
tangible media. Though it can apply to other platforms, one could simplify it to my own 
definition by narrowing it to Roblox.

iii. 	So, we have a simple definition of a myth: one or more characters directly 
associated with one or more games. A definition is not all we need in this community, and 
that may be why we struggle to achieve one. What we really need to deal with is how we 
determine the quality of a myth, what makes a myth, which can be used by groups for 
ranking, and for the hunters themselves, for their ideas of myths. – 

