1.2. What is a Hunter

i. 	Where before, we had to search far and wide for a fitting answer for what a myth 
was, a simple conclusion has already taken place for hunters. A hunter engages in myths 
of any sort; if a myth is an artist, then a hunter is an observer or a critic. Here, there is 
not as much detail in rankings for hunting; a hunter is simply one who loves to play myth 
games. The community wiki defines a hunter as someone who looks through profiles and 
games of a myth to come to a conclusion about the myth itself. A hunter is defined this 
way so that it can apply to anyone in the community, and so we can better see what 
makes a good hunter; everyone knows what a hunter is because everyone is a hunter, 
even some beyond our community borders. 

ii. 	One of the most important parts of the community is ranking in groups, how you 
compare with others, where your quality compared to others is visible. For hunters, 
these ranks tend to be determined by attending hunts, and beyond that requirement, 
ranks are then determined based on popularity and connection to the group itself. To 
me, this makes sense, though I’ve never truly been a hunter. I believe everyone in the 
community is a hunter, but I’ve never applied for any hunter ranks; all of my hunting 
has taken place as a myth. The quality of a hunter, to me, can fit this definition, but a 
hunter is not just joining hunts on time and being social. A hunter tends to be deeply 
skilled; this quality could be determined by testing applicants. A hunter is also engaged 
in the myths themselves, reaching out, speaking with them, and potentially documenting 
them; these seemingly are rarely taken into account rank-wise. Aside from group 
ranking or in-hunt quality, a hunter’s effect on the community can reach far, maybe 
starting a group, popularizing a myth, or forming content on myths. Hunters are not 
devoid of creativity; they use it for off-platform creation like videos, documentation, 
Discord, or they reach out to others who will engage in the myth community to 
potentially popularize it.

