iii. 	Though myths feel so separate from others, there are similar forms and 
communities. Something I’ve observed in some video, game, and music communities 
that surround known creator(s) is that the people tend to form a story around them. For 
public figures, their story is their life, and the parts of their life that went into their 
creations, communities can form around those stories, notably in times when the creator 
is not active. This is notable because it displays some yearning for the qualities of a 
myth, a character and their chosen media, like a game. On the creative side, where 
people form characters to hold their art, it can show that myth-like art can form 
anywhere, but it never forms a community of artists and investigative observers. For 
example, Lemony Snicket and the associated A Series of Unfortunate Events, where the 
book series is credited to the character, Lemony Snicket. Some photographers may use 
characters to have photos surround them, some music artists use characters to associate 
with albums, and even YouTube channels can surround characters, yet they all collect 
their own followings rather than have a community that encompasses more than one 
work. The closest art which can be associated with the myth community is the ARG 
community, as many consider Roblox ARGs as myths and vice versa. An ARG associates 
a character, a story, and a slow uncovering of a world with a chosen platform on the 
internet, which is exactly what a myth attempts to provide. It separates from myths, on 
Roblox specifically, as a game is not explicitly associated with an ARG. ARGs generally 
provide their story on a variety of platforms, whereas myths tend to stick on Roblox, 
straying out for some part of their game. Another idea, more centered on the myth 
community, is that we are a community of role-players who also construct the world(s) 
around us to fit our stories, which is a connection to look at. My wish is that you take all 
of these into account; they all apply much wider than the myth community, and we can 
take some of what they display into our own hands to boost the community further.
